cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Governance-Aware Evidence Fusion for Data-Quality Decisions: An Implemented Multi-Domain Evaluation of Anomaly Coverage and Review-Burden Trade-offs"
message: "If you use this repository in your research, please cite the accompanying manuscript and software artifact."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Kallam
    given-names: Ramesh Babu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5220-1775"

repository-code: "https://github.com/kallamrameshbabu/governance-aware-hybrid-data-quality"
license: Apache-2.0

keywords:
  - Data Quality
  - Data Governance
  - Evidence Fusion
  - Anomaly Detection
  - Decision Policy
  - Review Burden
  - Auditability
  - Lakehouse-Compatible Architecture

abstract: >
  An implemented governance-aware decision layer that combines deterministic
  rule risk, detector consensus, detector voting, and evidence uncertainty.
  The artifact evaluates a calibrated detection operating point and a full
  governed-routing operating point across 63 controlled experiments in
  finance, healthcare, and retail.

version: "2.0.0"
date-released: 2026-08-02
